---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import ButtonGroupDemo from "../../components/ButtonGroupDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Button Group"
  description="Joins related buttons, text cells, and separators into one control."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Button Group</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Joins related buttons into one control. Use it for pagers, steppers, split
    actions, and toolbars.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><ButtonGroupDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Button Group usage"
      code={`import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import {
  ButtonGroup,
  ButtonGroupSeparator,
  ButtonGroupText,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button-group";

<ButtonGroup aria-label="Pages">
  <Button variant="outline" disabled={page === 1}>Previous</Button>
  <ButtonGroupSeparator />
  <Button variant="outline" disabled={page === 3}>Next</Button>
</ButtonGroup>

<ButtonGroup orientation="vertical" aria-label="Quantity">
  <ButtonGroupText>Quantity: {quantity}</ButtonGroupText>
  <Button variant="outline" aria-label="Add one"><Plus /></Button>
</ButtonGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>ButtonGroup</code> renders a <code>div</code> with <code
        >role="group"</code
      >. <code>orientation</code> is <code>"horizontal"</code>, the default, or
      <code>"vertical"</code>. Direct children with a <code>data-slot</code>,
      such as Sprout buttons, lose their inner corners and the border where they
      meet. The outer corners use <code>--sprout-radius-control</code> for every button
      size.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ButtonGroupText</code> is a muted cell for a label or value. It accepts
      <code>render</code>, so it can be an <code>output</code> or a
      <code>label</code>. Icons inside it are 16px unless they have a size
      class.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>ButtonGroupSeparator</code> is a <code>Separator</code> with the
      <code>"input"</code> tone. It runs across the group, so it is <code
        >"vertical"</code
      > by default and must be <code>"horizontal"</code> in a vertical group. Use
      it between filled buttons, which have no border of their own.
    </p>
    <p>
      A group that holds other groups spaces them 8px apart. A direct
      <code>input</code> child grows to fill the free space. <code
        >buttonGroupVariants({"{ orientation }"})</code
      > returns the same class names for other elements.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Give each group an <code>aria-label</code> that names what it controls. Every
      button stays in the tab order, and a focused button draws its ring above its
      neighbors. Icon-only buttons need their own <code>aria-label</code>.
      Render a changing value with <code>render={"{<output />}"}</code> so screen
      readers hear it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Color changes follow the theme in 120ms and stop when reduced motion is
      requested. In forced colors mode text cells keep a visible border.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Text cells use <code>--sprout-secondary</code>, <code>--sprout-text</code
      >, and <code>--sprout-input</code>. Separators use <code
        >--sprout-input</code
      >. Radius follows <code>--sprout-radius-control</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
